The report is ready: `C:\Users\rafae\Documents\ccrcc-graphrag\reports\ccrcc_report.html`. The final check found 0 unsupported claims out of 118. One cells paragraph was first dropped because a value lacked its evidence id; I added the citation and re-ran.

1. **CA9 has the strongest and most robust convergent evidence.** It is up in tumour (RNA log2FC 6.312, protein 2.269), replicates in TCGA-KIRC, is still up after correcting for tumour purity, and is carried by tumour cells in both single-cell datasets. Girentuximab has reached phase 3. It is not prognostic and not a dependency, so it suits an antibody, radioligand or imaging approach.
2. **NNMT is the best combined target and biomarker.** It is tumour-intrinsic and prognostic (Cox log HR 0.301), and it holds in every validation layer: confirmatory proteomics, the second single-cell dataset and the literature. It has no drug, so as a target it is a small-molecule hypothesis.
3. **CD70 and SCARB1 come next, each with a caveat.** CD70 has clinical antibodies and the best antibody-drug-conjugate (ADC) suitability score among the known targets (0.746), but 0.654 of its tumour transcripts come from immune cells and the two single-cell datasets disagree on which cells carry it. SCARB1 is the target whose rank changes least under re-weighting (top 10 in 0.968 of draws), but it has no literature or drug.
4. **The leading biomarkers mark loss of normal kidney tubule identity.** PSAT1, PCK1, ALDH6A1, ALDOB and SLC22A8 are lost in tumour and prognostic; PSAT1 and PCK1 also replicate in confirmatory proteomics. EPAS1 (belzutifan) is the only candidate with a selective DepMap dependency, and it is borderline.
5. **The clinical layers add caveats rather than confirmation.** No gene separates the IMmotion150 treatment arms, and no convergent target is a cell-line dependency. Some coverage is missing: CA9 and CD70 could not be tested in the confirmatory cohort, and HK2 was not checked there, so the report does not repeat the earlier note that HK2 fails to replicate. STRING interactions were not queried.

